---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"leds\", \"theme\", \"apply\"])"
---
Apply a theme file, live, with no reboot: first its custom colours, then its lights profile fields. The lights profile becomes the one that runs. RAM only unless --save. gamepadii backs up the colours and the profile first. The custom colours are global: the other lights profiles that use colours 14 to 29 change too

Usage: gamepadii leds theme apply [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          The theme file, or - for standard input

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --profile <N>
          The lights profile to write, 0 to 3. Default: the one that runs

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --save
          Also save it to flash. Don't use this each time a game starts: each save writes the flash

      --no-backup
          Don't back up the colours and the lights profile first

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
